    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <h1 style="font-size: 24pt;">5.0 OPERATION</h1>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">
            The timing diagram of <span data-field="product_name">{{ product_name }}</span> is shown. To start measurement, Trig of SR04 must receive a pulse of high (<span data-field="pulse_high_duration">{{ pulse_high_duration }}</span>) for at least <span data-field="pulse_high_time">{{ pulse_high_time }}</span>, this will initiate the sensor will transmit out 8 cycle of ultrasonic burst at <span data-field="ultrasonic_frequency">{{ ultrasonic_frequency }}</span> and wait for the reflected ultrasonic burst. When the sensor detected ultrasonic from receiver, it will set the Echo pin to high (<span data-field="echo_high_duration">{{ echo_high_duration }}</span>) and delay for a period (width) which proportion to distance. To obtain the distance, measure the width (Ton) of Echo pin.
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 30px; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">
            Time = Width of Echo pulse, in uS (micro second)
            <br>
            Distance in centimeters = Time / 58
            <br>
            Distance in inches = Time / 148
            <br>
            Or you can utilize the speed of sound, which is 340m/s
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px; text-align: center;">
        <div style="display: inline-block; text-align: center;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 14pt;">Signal</h3>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #000; padding: 10px; display: inline-block;">
                <p style="margin: 0;">10uS TTL to signal pin</p>
                <div style="height: 30px; background-color: #ccc; margin-top: 5px;"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: inline-block; text-align: center; margin-left: 50px;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 14pt;">Echo back</h3>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #000; padding: 10px; display: inline-block;">
                <p style="margin: 0;">pulse width corresponds to distance (about 150uS-25ms, 38ms if no obstacle)</p>
                <div style="height: 30px; background-color: #ccc; margin-top: 5px;"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px; font-size: 10pt;">
        Formula:
        <br>
        pulse width (uS)/58 = distance (cm)
        <br>
        pulse width (uS)/148 = distance (inch)
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px; font-size: 10pt;">
        Ultrasonic Transducer will issue <span data-field="ultrasonic_frequency">{{ ultrasonic_frequency }}</span> pulse
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px; border: 1px solid #f00; padding: 15px; font-size: 10pt;">
        <p>Note:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 10px;">
            <li>Please connect the GND pin first before supplying power to VCC.</li>
            <li>Please make sure the surface of object to be detect should have at least <span data-field="min_detection_distance">{{ min_detection_distance }}</span> better performance.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
